## The Unit — LUMIS, The Pale Cave Sprite

Lumis is a small bioluminescent cave creature roughly the size of a cat — pale, faintly translucent, with wide dark eyes and thin limbs that end in soft luminous pads. It does not speak. It does not fight. It moves constantly, and it is very good at hiding in places where it shouldn't fit.

It has survived in Skullhollow for a long time. It knows the tunnels. It does not know what the Horsemen are.

**Lumis — Stats:**

| Stat | Value |
|---|---|
| HP | 40 |
| AC | 12 |
| Speed | 40ft (can pass through gaps as small as 6 inches) |
| Passive Perception | 16 |
| Passive Stealth | 18 |

**Lumis's Movement Pattern — Fixed Circuit:**
Lumis follows a looping route through the maze's major corridors in a counterclockwise circuit. The full circuit takes approximately **90 minutes** at its standard pace. It does not deviate unless a Horseman is within 60ft of it — then it immediately teleports to a random room at least 10 rooms away and resumes the circuit from there.

**DM Note:** Mark Lumis's position on your map each 15 minutes. Players who successfully track it (DC 14 Survival or DC 12 Perception in a room Lumis recently passed through) can intercept rather than chase.

**If a Horseman Reaches Lumis:**
- Lumis takes **2d10 damage**
- Lumis immediately teleports to a random distant room (DM rolls d6 for quadrant)
- If Lumis reaches 0 HP, the floor fails for ALL parties simultaneously

**Lumis's Trust:**
Lumis will not approach characters it has not seen before. However, if a character has been within 30ft of it without attacking for 2 consecutive rounds, Lumis will cautiously approach and follow that character for up to 10 minutes before resuming its circuit. This effectively lets a party escort it through a section of the maze.

