### HORSEMAN I — CONQUEST *(White Horse)*
*"He does not conquer by force. He conquers by making you believe you've already lost."*

**Starting Position:** Northwest quadrant of the maze.

| Stat | Mounted | Unmounted |
|---|---|---|
| AC | 18 | 14 |
| HP | 120 | 80 |
| Speed | 60ft | 30ft |
| Attack | Vorpal Lance: +8, 2d10+5 piercing + DC 15 Con or be Stunned 1 round | Silver Bow: +6, 1d8+4 piercing |

**Mounted Special — Crown of Inevitability:** While mounted, all creatures within 30ft must succeed a DC 15 Wisdom save at the start of their turn or have their movement halved and cannot take the Dash action.

**Weakness — Humility of the Crown:**
Conquest is bound by an ancient rule: a crowned ruler who willingly kneels before him cannot be harmed by him. If a player character is wearing any crown, circlet, or headpiece (including makeshift ones) and uses their action to kneel and speak aloud *"I acknowledge your victory,"* Conquest is **Stunned for 3 rounds** and his horse rears back, requiring a DC 14 Athletics check to control. On a failed check, the horse bucks him and he is dismounted.

Conquest will not attack a character who has knelt to him — only pursue Lumis. He considers it beneath him to strike the defeated.

**Killing the Mount (White Horse):**
White Horse AC 14, HP 40. It is proud and will not flee — but if it takes more than 20 damage in a single round, it rears uncontrollably and Conquest must make a DC 14 Strength save or be thrown.

**Clues that reveal this weakness:** Look for clues tagged **[C1]** in the room tables.

