### HORSEMAN II — WAR *(Red Horse)*
*"He does not need a reason. He needs a target."*

**Starting Position:** Northeast quadrant of the maze.

| Stat | Mounted | Unmounted |
|---|---|---|
| AC | 17 | 13 |
| HP | 140 | 90 |
| Speed | 50ft | 30ft |
| Attack | Greatsword of Ruin: +9, 2d6+6 slashing + on crit deals max damage | Thrown Axe: +7, 1d12+5 slashing, range 30/90 |

**Mounted Special — Tide of Battle:** When War hits a creature, all other creatures within 15ft must succeed a DC 14 Strength save or be pushed 10ft in a random direction and take 1d6 bludgeoning from the shockwave.

**Weakness — The White Banner:**
War cannot strike a creature carrying a White Banner — any white cloth tied to a weapon or pole and held aloft. This is an ancient compact. While the banner is raised, War halts and his horse stops moving. He will wait. If the banner is lowered, the compulsion immediately ends. The banner must be held as an action each round to maintain the effect.

A makeshift White Banner (DC 10 Investigation to construct from available cloth) counts. War recognizes the symbol regardless of craftsmanship.

**Killing the Mount (Red Horse):**
Red Horse AC 15, HP 50. It attacks any creature that comes within 5ft of War, dealing 1d8+3 hooves on a hit (+5). Killing it causes War to howl with rage — he gains advantage on all attacks for 3 rounds but takes a −2 AC penalty (fury and grief, simultaneously).

**Clues that reveal this weakness:** Look for clues tagged **[C2]** in the room tables.

