### HORSEMAN III — FAMINE *(Black Horse)*
*"He does not starve you. He makes you starve everything around you."*

**Starting Position:** Southeast quadrant of the maze.

| Stat | Mounted | Unmounted |
|---|---|---|
| AC | 15 | 11 |
| HP | 100 | 60 |
| Speed | 45ft | 25ft |
| Attack | Balance Scales (melee, reach 10ft): +7, 1d10+4 necrotic + target cannot benefit from healing for 1 minute | Touch of Drought: +5, 1d6+3 necrotic |

**Mounted Special — Withering Aura:** All food, potions, and consumable items within 20ft of Famine spoil and are destroyed at the start of his turn. (Magical items are immune. Standard rations and non-magical potions are not.)

**Weakness — Offering of Abundance:**
Famine is compelled to stop when presented with an offering of genuine food placed on the ground before him. He must spend 1 full round examining it — ancient compulsion, not choice. If the offering is a **Hearty Meal** or better quality food, he spends 2 rounds examining it and cannot move. If the food is poisoned (Medicine's Hollow oils count), the offering causes him 3d8 necrotic damage on examination and his horse flees — effectively dismounting him without combat.

**Killing the Mount (Black Horse):**
Black Horse AC 12, HP 35. It is the weakest of the mounts but it passively extends Famine's Withering Aura by 10ft. Killing it removes the aura entirely.

**Clues that reveal this weakness:** Look for clues tagged **[C3]** in the room tables.

