### HORSEMAN IV — DEATH *(Pale Horse)*
*"He does not hurry. He has already arrived."*

**Starting Position:** Southwest quadrant of the maze.

| Stat | Mounted | Unmounted |
|---|---|---|
| AC | 19 | 15 |
| HP | 160 | 110 |
| Speed | 40ft | 30ft |
| Attack | Scythe of Ending: +10, 2d8+7 necrotic + DC 16 Con save or drop to 0 HP (usable once per round, on a crit only) | Touch of Death: +8, 1d12+5 necrotic |

**Mounted Special — Deathly Stillness:** All creatures within 30ft of Death must succeed a DC 16 Wisdom save at the start of their turn or be Frightened until the start of their next turn.

**Immunity:** Death is immune to necrotic damage. He takes half damage from all sources while mounted.

**Weakness — Radiant Anchor:**
Death cannot willingly move through an area illuminated by **true radiant light** (Divine spells, the Godsliver Longsword's glow, or Medicine's Radiant-imbued Oil applied to a torch count). He must stop at the edge of any such light source. He can be kept stationary by maintaining a radiant light source between him and his destination.

Additionally, if struck by **10 or more radiant damage in a single hit**, Death is **knocked from his horse** automatically — the force disrupts his form.

**Killing the Mount (Pale Horse):**
Pale Horse AC 16, HP 60. It is immune to necrotic damage. Radiant damage deals double to it. Killing it causes Death's form to briefly destabilize — he becomes visible as a flickering, translucent figure and loses his Deathly Stillness aura for 5 rounds.

**Clues that reveal this weakness:** Look for clues tagged **[C4]** in the room tables.

