### HORSEMAN V — THE GILDED *(Gold Horse)*
*"He does not represent one catastrophe. He is the residue of all of them."*

**Starting Position:** Center of the maze — dormant. He does not move or act until the other four Horsemen have been defeated or simultaneously dismounted.

**Activation Condition:** When the fourth Horseman falls (or all four are dismounted at the same time), The Gilded activates. His Gold Horse rears and he turns toward Lumis's last known position.

| Stat | Mounted | Unmounted |
|---|---|---|
| AC | 20 | 16 |
| HP | 200 | 150 |
| Speed | 70ft | 40ft |
| Attack | All Four Attacks (alternates between Conquest's lance, War's sword, Famine's scales, Death's scythe — one per turn) | All Four Unmounted Attacks |

**Special — Inheritance of All:**
The Gilded inherits all weaknesses of the four defeated Horsemen simultaneously. A White Banner halts him. Radiant light blocks his path. Food offerings slow him. A kneeling crown-wearer stuns him.

If the party uses **all four weakness mechanics** against him in the same combat, he is forcibly dismounted with no Athletics check required — the accumulated weight of the compact breaks his mount entirely.

**Killing the Mount (Gold Horse):**
Gold Horse AC 18, HP 80. Immune to all damage unless all four previous mounts are already dead. If all four are dead, Gold Horse takes normal damage from all sources and has no special properties.

**Clues that reveal this weakness:** Look for clues tagged **[C5]** in the room tables.

