## THE ROOM CONTENT SYSTEM

When any party enters a room for the first time, roll on the **Master Room Table**. After a room has been entered once, its contents are fixed — a looted room stays looted, a triggered trap stays triggered.

**DM Note:** Track visited rooms on your map copy. Mark each with its result so you don't re-roll.

---

### MASTER ROOM TABLE — Roll d20

| d20 | Category | Sub-Table |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Enemy Fight** | Nothing. Cold stone. |
| 2 | **Empty with Tracks** | Lumis passed through recently. See Tracks entry. |
| 3–4 | **Junk** | Roll on Junk Table (d20) |
| 5–6 | **Junk** | Roll on Junk Table (d20) — roll twice, take both |
| 7–8 | **Useful Item** | Roll on Item Table (d12) |
| 9 | **Useful Item (Good)** | Roll on Item Table (d12) — roll twice, take higher number result |
| 10 | **Trap** | Roll on Trap Table (d10) |
| 11 | **Trick** | Roll on Trick Table (d10) |
| 12 | **Clue** | Roll on Clue Table (d10) |
| 13 | **Junk + Clue** | Roll once on each table |
| 14 | **Item + Trap** | Roll on both — item is present but so is the trap guarding it |
| 15 | **Item + Clue** | Roll on both — item and clue together |
| 16 | **Trick + Clue** | Roll on both — environmental trick, plus something written or carved nearby |
| 17 | **Trap + Junk** | Junk is bait for the trap |
| 18 | **Multiple Items** | Roll on Item Table (d12) three times. Take all three. |
| 19 | **Horseman Sign** | A Horseman was here recently. Roll d5 for which one. The room holds their lingering effect (see Horseman Signs). |
| 20 | **Special Room** | Roll on Special Room Table (d6) |

